 \, and staff meet to explore and critique artificial intelligence technolo
 gy\, and its implications for learners and researchers throughout the Brow
 n community. Learners of all levels and backgrounds are encouraged to shar
 e their experiences\, questions\, and ideas. This week’s topic: Challeng
 es and Advancements in AI Climate Reporting AI climate impact reporting ha
 s a reputation for being opaque. Is it possible to know the climate impact
 s of AI and its associated infrastructure? Are there things we can measure
  ourselves? In this talk we’ll explore some of the reasons why AI climat
 e accounting is so difficult\, areas and opportunities fo\nCategory: Free 
