BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Inside Gaza" Film Screening & Discussion — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261109T173000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261109T193000
DTSTAMP:20261109T222530Z
UID:b271fff8b209df374e5ddc1f9ed0@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Exhibition\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:The Institute for Middle East Studies is proud to announce a s
 creening of the award winning documentary Inside Gaza \, followed by remar
 ks from film director Hélène Lam Trong and featured journalist Mai Yaghi
 . Since the Hamas attack on 7 October 2023 and the Israeli reprisals that 
 followed\, international journalists and media have no access to the Gaza 
 Strip. Agence France-Presse journalists\, who were permanently stationed 
 in Gaza\, were among the last independent witnesses to the abuses committe
 d in the hellscape that Gaza has become. Featuring previously unseen foota
 ge and testimony from reporters Mai Yaghi and Adel Zaanoun\, as well as ph
 otojournalists Mahmud Hams and Mohammed Abed\, Inside G\nCategory: Exhibit
 ion\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/inside-gaza-film-scr
 eening-discussion
LOCATION:Elliott School of International Affairs\, 1957 E Street NW\, Wash
 ington\, DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/inside-gaza-film-screening-discussion
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Seminar - Capitalism in South Korea\, 1945-2025 — Washingto
 n\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261109T173000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261109T190000
DTSTAMP:20261109T222530Z
UID:f3e0dc98c6461fbcef67a1367cff@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Academic\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:How did South Korea’s rapid economic transformation shape it
 s democracy\, institutions\, and society? In his book\, Keun Lee examines 
 South Korea’s development since 1945 through a framework of compressed d
 evelopment\, decompression\, and convergence. He explores how rapid growth
  helped create a middle class that demanded political freedom\, and how IM
 F-led reforms following the Asian financial crisis reshaped the country’
 s economic trajectory. The seminar will examine the book's findings. Read 
 a full abstract here . About the Speaker Keun Lee is a Distinguished Profe
 ssor of Economics at Chung-Ang University and professor emeritus at Seoul 
 National University. He is a fellow at the Canadian Instit\nCategory: Acad
 emic\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/book-seminar-capita
 lism-in-south-korea-1945-2025
LOCATION:Elliott School of International Affairs\, 1957 E Street\, NW\, Wa
 shington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/book-seminar-capitalism-in-south-korea-
 1945-2025
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:gwu-arts
END:VEVENT
