 United States
DESCRIPTION:You’ve got your research question—now\, how do you actuall
 y find the sources you need? With hundreds of databases available\, where 
 should you start\, and how do you know if you’re searching effectively? 
 Join librarians as we tackle these challenges in our Find Research Materia
 ls Workshop. We’ll demystify the database landscape\, distinguishing bet
 ween broad discovery tools like BruKnow and discipline-specific databases 
 tailored to your field. You’ll practice translating your own keywords in
 to the controlled vocabulary that databases use\, and learn to identify 
 “seed articles” that can anchor and expand your research. This worksho
 p is designed to help undergraduate researchers develop strategic\, \nCate
 gory: Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.
 brown.edu/library/event/337713-research-fundamentals-find-research-materia
 ls
