CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Lectures\, Seminars and Workshops\,Providence\,
 United States
DESCRIPTION:Learn about git\, a powerful tool for keeping track of your wo
 rk (whether it’s code\, data\, writing/prose\, etc.) and collaborating w
 ith others - including future-you! This workshop assumes no prior knowledg
 e and introduces you to the popular version-control system git and its web
 -hosted counterpart\, GitHub. We will also explore use cases in digital sc
 holarship\, open educational resources (OER) for teaching\, and web develo
 pment as three areas where you can apply these skills. Registration is ope
 n to learners of all backgrounds. This workshop is part of a series hosted
  by the Center for Digital Scholarship (CDS)\, “The Bread of Butter of D
 igital Humanities: Common Tools and Methods in the Field.”\nCategory: Le
 ctures\, Seminars and Workshops\nOriginal listing: https://events.brown.ed
 u/library/event/336311-github-and-git-for-everyone
