CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:REFLECT traces the evolution of artist Cannuap Hanska Luger’
 s Mirror Shield Project . In 2016\, when the Dakota Access Pipeline threat
 ened the waters of his ancestral homelands\, Luger circulated a video demo
 nstrating how to make “mirror shields” from inexpensive materials. Con
 ceived during the Indigenous-led resistance at Standing Rock\, North Dakot
 a\, the tutorial functioned as a call to collective action\, an invitation
  for people across the country to stand in solidarity with the Water Prote
 ctors. Carried by Water Protectors in frontline actions and collective for
 mations\, the mirrored surfaces offered protection while redirecting the f
 ield of vision. More than a thousand mirror shields were c\nCategory: Arts
  & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/cannupa-hansk
 a-lugers-reflect
