CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Take a student-led tour of the exhibitions currently on view a
 t the Brady Art Gallery: "Unfossilizing African Art" and "Cracks and Refor
 ms". Unfossilizing African Art recontextualizes African material culture o
 bjects that have been held in the GW Collection for nearly 50 years. Led b
 y Assistant Professor Clement Akpang\, 59 students across four seminar cou
 rses conducted original research to deepen understanding of the collection
  and reconsider how these objects are interpreted and exhibited. Cracks & 
 Reforms: The 1920s Through the GW Collection examines a decade shaped by p
 olitical upheaval\, social transformation\, migration\, modernization\, an
 d cultural redefinition. This exhibition\, developed\nCategory: Arts & Cul
 ture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/brady-art-gallery-t
 our-unfossilizing-african-art-and-cracks-reforms
