SUMMARY:National Symphony Orchestra: The Nutcracker & Cinderella — Washi
 ngton\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261121T200000
DTSTAMP:20261109T222530Z
UID:378f632e2a53be3fb31fe6eaff51@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Be moved by two treasured fairy tales through the music of Tch
 aikovsky and Prokofiev\, conducted by Marie Jacquot in her NSO debut. Tcha
 ikovskys The Nutcracker Suite brings Clara\, the Sugar Plum Fairy\, and an
  enchanted Christmas Eve party to the concert stage\, while Prokofievs Cin
 derella Suite reimagines the timeless story with music that is playful and
  packed with clever turns. Between the ballets\, Jorge Federico Osorio cas
 ts a different kind of spell in Mozarts Piano Concerto No. 21\, famous for
  its slow\, haunting second movement. Three beloved works\, three worlds o
 f magic! There is a ticket limit of 8 tickets per person and per credit ca
 rd on this event.\nCategory: Arts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://cal
 endar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcracker-cinderella
LOCATION:Lisner Auditorium\, 730 21st Street NW\, Washington DC 20052
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/national-symphony-orchestra-the-nutcrac
 ker-cinderella
